  "headline": "D.C. Circuit blocks IRS procedure used to share taxpayer addresses with ICE",
  "bounded_summary": "The D.C. Circuit upheld an injunction against the IRS data-exchange procedure used to provide taxpayer address information to ICE, finding that the procedure failed to satisfy federal tax-privacy requirements. Reuters reported that the IRS had disclosed roughly 47,000 taxpayer addresses after ICE sought information on approximately 1.28 million people.",
